		Manual: {
			Title: === Levy Field Manual ===
			Body:
				'''
				Your junk becomes a garrison. Here is how.

				1. Settlement. Build a Barracks and an Armory at a Work Bench, side by side in your town. Town NPCs whose homes are within 120 tiles of the Barracks become its settlement. You do not house soldiers; they live at the Barracks. House your town NPCs as you always would. Each one adds manpower.

				2. The Armory. Throw spare weapons, armor, ammo and potions into it. Soldiers arm themselves from its issue rows, best gear first. Soldiers wield nearly any weapon a player can: guns, bows, magic, swords, spears and shortswords, whips, boomerangs, yoyos and flails, summon staves and sentries, held weapons like the Last Prism, and thrown weapons and bombs. Put what you want issued first into the issue slots at the top. Soldiers also draw from storage, best first.

				3. Regulars. Right-click the Barracks and enlist. Regulars are named soldiers who follow you anywhere. They cost a muster fee up front and a daily wage at dawn, both from the Barracks treasury, so deposit coins there. Keep it full or they desert. The Kit button on a Regular's row shows their gear; put an item in a slot by hand and it stays on them until you take it out.

				4. Militia. Hold the War Horn and left-click to call up the whole town to hold the walls. They arm from the Armory, fight at the settlement, and stand down when the invasion or Blood Moon ends. Manpower is the limit, and it drains as they fall.

				5. Orders. Right-click the War Horn for the radial. Keys: Y follow, U hold, I return, O hold fire, P mobilize, K rally, N army overview. The radial also has Search & destroy (roam outward and hunt, never into contact), Free rein (the same hunt with no leash: they range across the whole region on their own, out of your sight, and follow the fighting), Spread out (a wide loose line against area attacks) and Focus attack (click an enemy and the squad fires on it until it dies, or click a critter or a spot and the squad attacks it).

				6. Growth. Feed soldiers Life Crystals for more health, or leave Life Crystals, Life Fruit and Mana Crystals in the Armory and they take them on their own. Promote Regulars to Man-at-Arms after any mechanical boss, Champion after Golem. Accessories you give them do what they would on you; wings take a slot.

				7. Drones. They need the Mechanization mod. Craft A Guide to Engineering at an Anvil and study it. Each Barracks then launches combat drones, one for every spare ranged or magic weapon in its Armory, up to 10. A drone patrols above the Barracks, mounts the weapon and fires it at nearby enemies. Right-click a drone, or press the drone key, to recall it to its pad and hand its weapon back to the Armory. A destroyed drone returns its weapon too. Soldiers always take weapons first; drones only get what the army can spare.

				They are morons. They die like players. They cost money. Watch them fight.
				'''
		}

